# Two modules that read nothing of each other, and what decides which one initializes
# first.
#   zerg build examples/1g/initorder/main.zg
# Expected output:
#   ada-const     — `project:ada` sorts before `project:zebra`
#   zebra-const
#   3
#
# THE IMPORTS BELOW ARE IN THE OTHER ORDER on purpose. Top-level constants initialize in
# dependency order, and neither of these reads the other, so the graph leaves them
# unordered — and what breaks that tie is the CANONICAL MODULE NAME, not the order the
# import lines were written (docs/runtime/package.md). Swap the two lines and the output
# does not move; that is the whole of this example.
import (
	"./zebra"
	"./ada"
)

fn main() {
	print zebra.Z + ada.A
}
